# This suite's Kconfig: one symbol of its own, plus the whole application one.
#
# The symbol exists because the two properties of RFO-B12 do not fit in a single
# image. The display thread reads device_is_ready() ONCE, 500 ms after boot;
# denying readiness after that does not make it reconsider, and denying it
# earlier makes the healthy path unmeasurable. So the difference between the two
# scenes has to exist at boot, and it comes from here.
config REFLOW_TEST_DENY_PANEL
	bool "Deny the chosen display's readiness before any thread runs"
	help
	  A POST_KERNEL SYS_INIT clears the chosen device's readiness so that the
	  display thread finds the panel unavailable - the RFO-B12 scenario.
	  Without it the suite measures the healthy path.

# The application Kconfig, whole: it brings the CONFIG_REFLOW_* menu and ends in
# `source "Kconfig.zephyr"`, so the tree is sourced exactly once. Sourcing
# `Kconfig.zephyr` directly here would lose every application symbol.
source "$(APPLICATION_SOURCE_DIR)/../../Kconfig"
